You’re not going to like this answer, but you should stop taking photos of strangers in their pants and underwear with your smartphone or any other device.

It is illegal under federal law (Title 18 U.S.C., Section 2256) as well as state laws across America—including California where we live here at The Daily Beast—to photograph someone without consent if they are “in a place where he/she has an expectation of privacy.” That means that even though there may be no one else around when you snap those pics, you still need permission from whoever owns what you’ve captured before posting them online!<h2>How do I know if I have been caught by a camera?</h2>

If you think you might have been photographed while out shopping or walking down the street, check these places first:

* Your home address book;
* Any social media accounts linked directly through Facebook Messenger chat windows;
